1. Data & Integration Layer
Before you can sell effectively, your systems need to talk to each other without stuttering.

[ ] Centralized Product Information Management (PIM): Do you have a "single source of truth" for product descriptions, images, and specs across all channels?

[ ] Real-Time Inventory Sync: Can your system update stock levels across web, mobile, and physical stores within seconds of a sale?

[ ] Unified Customer View: Is customer data (loyalty points, purchase history, preferences) consolidated into a single profile accessible by marketing and in-store staff?

[ ] API-First Architecture: Are your systems modular? Can you easily plug in a new shipping provider or payment gateway via API?

2. Omnichannel Infrastructure
Modern retail is "phygital"—the line between physical and digital is gone.

[ ] Headless Commerce Readiness: Is your "back-end" (logic/data) decoupled from your "front-end" (what the user sees), allowing you to update the website without breaking the checkout?

[ ] Flexible Fulfillment: Does your system support BOPIS (Buy Online, Pick Up In-Store), BORIS (Buy Online, Return In-Store), and Ship-from-Store?

[ ] Mobile-First UX: Is the checkout process optimized for a one-handed thumb tap?

[ ] Edge Computing: If you have physical stores, do you have enough local bandwidth to support IoT devices, smart mirrors, or mobile POS systems?

3. Security & Compliance
Trust is a retail currency. If you lose it, the foundation crumbles.

[ ] PCI DSS Compliance: Are your payment processing systems fully compliant with latest standards?

[ ] Data Privacy (GDPR/CCPA): Do you have clear consent management for tracking cookies and marketing emails?

[ ] Cybersecurity Protocols: Is Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) mandatory for all employees accessing the backend?

[ ] Disaster Recovery Plan: Do you have a "warm" backup of your site/data that can go live if your primary server fails?

4. Performance & Scalability
A foundation is useless if it cracks under the pressure of a Black Friday rush.

[ ] Cloud Scalability: Does your hosting auto-scale to handle 10x your normal traffic?

[ ] Core Web Vitals: Does your site load in under 2 seconds? (Every 100ms delay can drop conversions by 7%).

[ ] Analytics Tracking: Are you tracking more than just sales? (e.g., heatmaps, cart abandonment triggers, and search-to-click ratios).
